<!doctype html>
<%# Generated by scripts/catalog.rb from scripts/ramp_designs.rb; edit the template, not docs/seattle/curb-ramps/index.html. -%>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Seattle Curb Ramp Designs</title>
<meta name="description" content="Every curb ramp design in the City of Seattle Standard Plans, illustrated: perpendicular, parallel, directional, diagonal, blended transitions and island cut-throughs, with when each is used.">
<link rel="icon" href="../../favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="../../apple-touch-icon.png">
<meta name="theme-color" content="#1f2a24">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<meta property="og:title" content="Seattle's curb ramp designs, illustrated">
<meta property="og:description" content="Every curb ramp design in Seattle's Standard Plans, illustrated, with when the city uses each one.">
<meta property="og:url" content="https://olivierlacan.github.io/trebuche/seattle/curb-ramps/">
<meta property="og:image" content="https://olivierlacan.github.io/trebuche/og.png">
<meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="../../site.css">
<style>
  .designs { display: grid; gap: 18px; }
  .design { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.15fr); gap: 22px; align-items: start;
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; padding: 18px; scroll-margin-top: 16px; }
  .design img { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 14px rgba(0,0,0,.18); }
  .design h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 22px; }
  .design .code { margin: 0 0 2px; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--accent); letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .design p { margin: 0 0 10px; }
  .design ul { margin: 0 0 12px; padding-left: 20px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .design li { margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .design .links { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 6px 18px; margin: 0; font-weight: 600; }
  @media (max-width: 720px) { .design { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; padding: 14px; } }
  .jump { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 24px; list-style: none; }
  .family { margin-top: 40px; }
  .family > h3 { font-size: 24px; margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .family > .sheet { margin: 0 0 14px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .caveat { font-size: 14px; color: var(--muted); border-left: 3px solid #f0d37a; padding-left: 10px; }
  .design h4 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 20px; }
  .design ul strong { color: var(--fg); font-weight: 600; }
  .jump a { display: inline-block; padding: 6px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface); text-decoration: none; font-size: 15px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a href="../../" aria-label="Trebuche home"><img class="hero-logo" src="../../logo.svg" width="76" height="76" alt=""></a>
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="../../">Trebuche</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><a href="../">Seattle</a><span aria-hidden="true">›</span><span aria-current="page">Curb ramp designs</span></nav>
    <h1>Seattle's curb ramp designs</h1>
    <p class="lede">Seattle's Standard Plans describe eight types of curb ramp, most drawn more than one way, for <%= DESIGNS.size %> designs in all. Here's what each one looks
      like and when the city uses it, so you can picture what might fit at your corner.</p>
    <div class="ctas">
      <a class="btn primary" href="../../ar/">Place one at your corner in AR</a>
      <a class="btn" href="../#ask">How to ask the city</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="designs-h">
    <h2 id="designs-h">The designs</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">Drawn to scale from the
      <a href="<%= PDF %>#page=209">2026 City of Seattle Standard Plans</a> (422a to 422h, with the general rules in
      <a href="<%= PDF %>#page=218">422k</a>), for Seattle's standard 6 inch curb. As in our logo, the curb is drawn
      taller than it is so you can see it. Corners are drawn with one curb radius each, and real ones vary. SDOT
      engineers pick the design for each corner, and your request doesn't need to name one. Every design can be
      placed at your corner <a href="../../ar/">in AR</a>.</p>
    <ul class="jump">
<%- families.each do |fam, ds| -%>
      <li><a href="#<%= fam %>"><%= fam.upcase %> <%= FAMILIES[fam].downcase %></a></li>
<%- end -%>
    </ul>
<%- families.each do |fam, ds| -%>
    <section class="family" id="<%= fam %>" aria-labelledby="<%= fam %>-h">
      <h3 id="<%= fam %>-h">Type <%= fam.upcase %>: <%= FAMILIES[fam].downcase %></h3>
      <p class="sheet"><%= ds.size > 1 ? "#{ds.size} versions on " : "" %><a href="<%= PDF %>#page=<%= ds[0][:plan] %>">Standard Plan <%= fam %></a></p>
      <div class="designs">
<%- ds.each do |d| -%>
        <article class="design" id="<%= d[:id] %>">
          <img src="<%= d[:id] %>.svg" width="160" height="100" alt="<%= alt_text(d) %>" loading="lazy">
          <div>
<%- if d[:variant] -%>
            <p class="code"><%= d[:variant] %></p>
<%- end -%>
            <h4><%= d[:name] %></h4>
            <p><%= d[:when] %></p>
            <ul>
<%- d[:specs].each do |a, b| -%>
              <li><strong><%= a %></strong> <%= b %></li>
<%- end -%>
            </ul>
<%- if caveat(d) -%>
            <p class="caveat"><%= caveat(d) %></p>
<%- end -%>
            <p class="links"><a href="../../ar/?type=<%= d[:id] %>">See it in AR →</a><a href="<%= PDF %>#page=<%= d[:plan] %>">Plan <%= fam %> →</a></p>
          </div>
        </article>
<%- end -%>
      </div>
    </section>
<%- end -%>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap" aria-labelledby="rules-h">
    <h2 id="rules-h">What every design shares</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Two ramps per corner, one for each crossing, unless nothing else fits (422k).</li>
      <li>Ramp runs no steeper than 8.3% and at least 4 ft wide, with cross slopes of 2% or less.</li>
      <li>A Federal Safety Yellow warning panel of truncated domes, 2 ft deep, where the ramp meets the street.</li>
      <li>Poles, hydrants and signs at least 1 ft from the ramp and landing, and no utility covers in them.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="small">Not shown: Plan 456b's temporary ramps for construction detours, and Plan 433's waste access ramp,
      which isn't for pedestrians.</p>
  </section>
</main>

<footer class="foot">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="foot-brand"><img src="../../logo.svg" width="40" height="40" alt=""><span>Trebuche</span></div>
    <p class="small">Illustrations drawn from the City of Seattle Standard Plans by <code>scripts/catalog.rb</code>,
      in the style of the Trebuche logo.</p>
  </div>
</footer>
</body>
</html>
